{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WV1rumn9PBhx83igFccj4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GTDGmbH */\n2\t/* Copyright 2020-2025 by GTD GmbH. */\n3\t\n4\t/**\n5\t *\n6\t * This family of functions computes the next floating-point value after\n7\t * :math:`x` in direction of :math:`y`.\n8\t *\n9\t * Synopsis\n10\t * ========\n11\t *\n12\t * .. code-block:: c\n13\t *\n14\t *     #include <math.h>\n15\t *     float nexttowardf(float x, long double y);\n16\t *     double nexttoward(double x, long double y);\n17\t *     long double nexttowardl(long double x, long double y);\n18\t *\n19\t * Description\n20\t * ===========\n21\t *\n22\t * ``nexttoward`` computes the next floating-point value after :math:`x` in\n23\t * direction of :math:`y`.\n24\t *\n25\t * ``nexttoward`` is functionally equivalent to :ref:`nextafter` but uses\n26\t * ``long double`` for the :math:`y` input. As the library only supports 64bit\n27\t * ``long double`` the procedure ``nexttoward`` is just calling\n28\t * :ref:`nextafter` as the types are the same, but for ``nexttowardf`` there is\n29\t * an actual difference as :math:`y` can be chosen to be so close to :math:`x`\n30\t * that it would be the same value in ``float`` but isn't in (effectively)\n31\t * ``double``. This results in ``nexttowardf`` having it's own implementation\n32\t * while ``nexttoward`` does not.\n33\t *\n34\t * Mathematical Function\n35\t * =====================\n36\t *\n37\t * .. math::\n38\t *\n39\t *    nexttoward(x, y) = \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} y, & x = y \\\\ \\text{min} \\{z | z \\in \\mathbb{F} \\wedge z > x\\}, & x < y \\\\ \\text{max} \\{z | z \\in \\mathbb{F} \\wedge z < x\\}, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.\n40\t *\n41\t * Returns\n42\t * =======\n43\t *\n44\t * ``nexttoward`` returns the the next floating-point value after :math:`x` in\n45\t * direction of :math:`y`.\n46\t *\n47\t * Exceptions\n48\t * ==========\n49\t *\n50\t * Raise ``overflow`` exception when the magnitude of :math:`x` is the largest\n51\t * finite value representable in the type and :math:`y` is infinite with the\n52\t * same sign as :math:`x`.\n53\t *\n54\t * .. May raise ``underflow`` exception.\n55\t *\n56\t * Output map\n57\t * ==========\n58\t *\n59\t * +--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+\n60\t * | nexttoward(x,y)          | x                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n61\t * +--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+\n62\t * | y                        | :math:`-Inf`             | :math:`<0`               | :math:`-0`               | :math:`+0`               | :math:`>0`               | :math:`+Inf`             | :math:`NaN`              |\n63\t * +==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+\n64\t * | :math:`-Inf`             | :math:`-Inf`             | :math:`nexttoward(x, y)` | max :math:`\\mathbb{S}^{-}`                          | :math:`nexttoward(x, y)` | :math:`nexttoward(x, y)` | :math:`qNaN`             |\n65\t * +--------------------------+--------------------------+                          +                                                     +                          +                          +                          +\n66\t * | :math:`<0`               | :math:`nexttoward(x, y)` |                          |                                                     |                          |                          |                          |\n67\t * +--------------------------+                          +                          +--------------------------+--------------------------+                          +                          +                          +\n68\t * | :math:`-0`               |                          |                          | :math:`y`                                           |                          |                          |                          |\n69\t * +--------------------------+                          +                          +                                                     +                          +                          +                          +\n70\t * | :math:`+0`               |                          |                          |                                                     |                          |                          |                          |\n71\t * +--------------------------+                          +                          +--------------------------+--------------------------+                          +                          +                          +\n72\t * | :math:`>0`               |                          |                          | min :math:`\\mathbb{S}^{+}`                          |                          |                          |                          |\n73\t * +--------------------------+                          +                          +                                                     +                          +--------------------------+                          +\n74\t * | :math:`+Inf`             |                          |                          |                                                     |                          | :math:`+Inf`             |                          |\n75\t * +--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+-------